                                <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
                            </svg>
                            <span>Use <code>int</code> for whole numbers, <code>double</code> for decimals, <code>decimal</code> for money.</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="takeaway">
                            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                                <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
                            </svg>
                            <span>Use <code>string</code> for text and <code>bool</code> for true/false values.</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="takeaway">
                            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                                <polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/>
                            </svg>
                            <span>The <code>var</code> keyword lets the compiler infer the type.</span>
                        </div>
