                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Practice Exercises</h2>
                    
                    <div class="exercise-box">
                        <h4>Exercise 3.1: Variable Declaration</h4>
                        <p>Create a program that stores and displays information about a book:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Title (string)</li>
                            <li>Author (string)</li>
                            <li>Year published (int)</li>
                            <li>Price (decimal)</li>
                            <li>Is available (bool)</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p>Display all the information in a nicely formatted way.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="exercise-box">
                        <h4>Exercise 3.2: Type Conversion</h4>
                        <p>Create a program that:</p>
                        <ol>
                            <li>Asks the user for their birth year</li>
                            <li>Converts the input to an integer</li>
                            <li>Calculates and displays their age</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p><strong>Bonus:</strong> Use <code>TryParse()</code> to handle invalid input gracefully.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="exercise-box">
                        <h4>Exercise 3.3: Temperature Converter</h4>
                        <p>Create a program that asks for a temperature in Celsius and converts it to Fahrenheit.</p>
                        <p><strong>Formula:</strong> F = (C × 9/5) + 32</p>
                        <p><strong>Hint:</strong> Be careful with integer vs floating-point division!</p>
                    </div>
